+{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"agent_message","text":"## **Constraint-Based Event Scheduler**\n\nI implemented a constraint-based scheduler in `src/scheduler.ts` (re-exported from `src/index.ts`).\n\n- `src/scheduler.ts` — full implementation\n- `src/index.ts` — named/default re-export plus type re-exports\n\n**Approach**\n\n- **Cycle detection** (`detectCycle`): DFS tri-coloring over the prerequisite graph; throws a `CycleError` for any cycle, including self-references like `A -> A`.\n- **Topological order** (`topoSort`): Kahn's algorithm so prerequisites are always decided before dependents; ties broken by shorter duration first to pack tightly and speed pruning.\n- **Candidate rooms**: filtered by capacity, with `preferredRoom` promoted to front (if capacity-feasible) so the search prefers it while still allowing fallback rooms.\n- **Branch-and-bound DFS**: at each event, try every feasible room using `earliestFit` (gap-aware interval packing); also try skipping the event. Pruning bounds by `placedCount + remaining` so dead branches are cut early. Final selection maximizes scheduled count, with preferred-room hits as a tiebreaker (`SCORE_WEIGHT`).\n- **Prerequisite handling**: an event's lower-bound start is `max(prereq.endTime + gap)`; if any prerequisite wasn't placed, the event is unschedulable.\n\n**Rules enforced**\n\n- Room capacity, time window, inter-event gap (default 15), prerequisite ordering + gap, preferred room (soft hint), cycle throwing, and batch maximization with `unscheduled` fallback.\n\n**Verification**\n\n- `npm run build` — compiles cleanly with `strict` TS.\n- `npm run lint` — 0 errors (removed unused interface and rewrote `while(true)` into `for(;;)` to satisfy `no-constant-condition`).\n- Ad-hoc `vitest` suite covering window/gap placement, capacity rejection, prerequisite + gap ordering, self-cycle and multi-cycle errors, preferred-room honoring, greedy-vs-optimal packing, and oversized-event unscheduling — all 8 passed.\n\n**Notes**\n\n- `npm install` rewrote `package-lock.json` to fill in missing entries; I left that change in place.\n- I removed the generated `dist/` directory after building to keep the tree clean; no source-only `tests/` dir exists in the repo so I didn't add a permanent test file. If you'd like, I can drop a `tests/scheduler.test.ts` with the sanity cases so `npm test` runs them persistently."}}
